Description: antinomie: capture ioctl arguments by their size, name more of them, and type reads of event descriptors
 An ioctl request outside the decoded set recorded only a gap. Its number
 usually encodes the argument's direction and size (_IOC_DIR, _IOC_SIZE):
 kernel/antinomie/recorder.c now records those bytes, opaque, up to 4096,
 at entry for _IOC_WRITE and at exit on success for _IOC_READ; a request
 whose number encodes neither keeps its gap. The socket interface requests
 (SIOCGIF*, SIOCSIF*), TUNSETIFF, SIOCGIFCONF with the ifreq array it fills,
 the loop device's status (LOOP_SET_STATUS64, LOOP_GET_STATUS64,
 LOOP_CONFIGURE), FICLONERANGE and the fsxattr pair are recorded by their
 layouts (ifreq, ifconf, loop_info64, loop_config, file_clone_range,
 fsxattr).
 .
 A read of an eventfd, timerfd, signalfd, inotify, fanotify or userfaultfd
 descriptor returns that kind's records; the read's buffer now names their
 layout (u64, signalfd_siginfo[], inotify_event[], fanotify_event_metadata[],
 uffd_msg[]), from the anonymous inode the file was made on.
 .
 epoll_ctl's event is recorded for an operation the kernel refuses too.
 .
 Contract revision 21.
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
